    {
      "name": "Book an appointment",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.environment.set(\"patientId\", \"pat-\" + pm.variables.replaceIn('{{$guid}}'));"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Parse the JSON response\r\nvar jsonData = pm.response.json();\r\n\r\n// Save the new appointment ID to your environment\r\npm.environment.set(\"appointmentId\", jsonData.appointmentId); \r\n"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\r\n    \"doctorId\": \"{{doctorId}}\",\r\n    \"patientId\": \"{{patientId}}\",\r\n    \"appointmentDate\": \"2026-10-06\",\r\n    \"startTime\": \"13:00:00\"\r\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{scheduling_url}}/api/appointments",
          "host": [
            "{{scheduling_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "appointments"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Books an appointment for a patient with the doctor configured in the previous steps.\n\nRun this after **Set a working schedule** and **Create pricing profile**, using the same Postman environment.\n\n**Prerequisites**\n\n- The Scheduling and Billing services and their required infrastructure are running.\n    \n- `scheduling_url` points to the Scheduling service.\n    \n- `doctorId` identifies the doctor configured in the previous steps.\n    \n\n**Request body**\n\n- `doctorId`: the doctor receiving the booking.\n    \n- `patientId`: a patient identifier generated by the pre-request script.\n    \n- `appointmentDate`: a future date on or after the schedule’s `validFrom` date.\n    \n- `startTime`: an available time within the doctor’s working hours. The full appointment must fit within a working shift.\n    \n\n**Scripts**  \nThe pre-request script generates and stores a new `patientId`. After a successful booking, the post-response script saves the returned `appointmentId` for subsequent requests.\n\n**Expected outcome**  \nThe appointment is created. Billing processes the booking event asynchronously to create its draft invoice."
      },
